A '''warlord''' was a military leader in charge of civilian territory.

==History==
===Republic Era===
Throughout [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]], the [[Hutt]] species controlled a criminal network<ref name="The Rising Storm" /> known as the [[Hutt Clan]],<ref name="HC Databank">{{Databank|hutt-clan|Hutt Clan}}</ref> otherwise known as the Hutt Cartel,<ref name="The Rising Storm" /> that stretched across numerous worlds<ref name="HC Databank" /> and outright controlled a segment of [[the galaxy]] known as [[Hutt Space]].<ref name="THR 5">[[The High Republic (2021) 5|''The High Republic'' (2021) 5]]</ref> At their best, the Hutts were known to act as warlords, while at their worst they were considered [[gangster]]s.<ref name="The Rising Storm" /> Throughout its history, the [[Galactic Republic]] fought with warlords and other enemies, such as the Hutts whenever the cartel made moves against the Republic.<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> At least after they had annexed a whole portion of the galaxy dubbed the [[Occlusion Zone]], the ranks of the [[Nihil]] [[Pirate|marauders]] included warlords, such as [[Melis Shryke]]. Furthermore, after the Nihil broadcasted the [[Pra-Tre Veter's execution|execution]] of [[Grand Master]] [[Pra-Tre Veter]], [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Lina Soh]] expressed her concerns that the public demonstration of the Republic's inability to protect its citizens would inspire countless petty warlords to begin carving up pieces of the galaxy into their own minor dominions.<ref name="Eye of Darkness" />

[[File:LulaZeenReunion-2023THRA1.png|thumb|left|300px|Zeen Mrala confronted the supposed rogue Nihil warlord Tartak Vil, only to discover the individual was really her lost love Lula Talisola]]
The amnesiac [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Lula Mrala-Talisola|Lula Talisola]] took up the life of a rogue Nihil<ref name="HRA 2023 3">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 3|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 3]]</ref> warlord named Tartak Vil after the [[destruction of Starlight Beacon]], establishing a mini-fiefdom on the moon [[Bracront]]<ref name="HRA 2023 1">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 1|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 1]]</ref> just outside the Nihil-controlled Occlusion Zone. Looking to keep herself alive<ref name="HRA 2023 2">[[The High Republic Adventures (2023) 2|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2023) 2]]</ref> and finding that people obeyed her without even asking when she wore stolen Nihil garb, even though she had no memory of what the Nihil were, she took up the life of "Tartak Vil" to stay safe.<ref name="HRA 2023 3" /> By keeping a low profile and taking advantage of the [[Galactic Republic]]'s focus on the wider Nihil organization, "Vil" was able to maintain "his" rule on Bracront with the support of the locals, who "Vil" protected and supported as a noble leader. The [[Mission to Bracront|arrival]] of Talisola's lost love [[Zeen Mrala-Talisola|Zeen Mrala]]<ref name="HRA 2023 1" /> helped Talisola move on from that life<ref name="HRA 2023 2" /> and awaken her old memories.<ref name="HRA 2023 3" /> After the conclusion of the [[Nihil conflict|hostilities]] between the Nihil and the Galactic Republic and the surrender of the former, some worlds that had been held within the Occlusion Zone were controlled by Nihil warlords.<ref name="HRTotJ">''[[The High Republic: Trials of the Jedi]]''</ref>

The planet [[Kalee]], [[homeworld]] of the [[Kaleesh]], produced warlords. Those warlords were idolized by a [[Youngling|young]] [[Grievous]], who observed them return home with spoils of war from those they had conquered.<ref name= "The Dark Side">''[[Star Wars: The Dark Side]]''</ref> Grievous would, in time, become a warlord himself at the head of the [[Izvoshra]],<ref name="BDOWD" /> and his name terrified his opponents.<ref name="Hyperspace Stories: Grievous">''[[Hyperspace Stories: Grievous]]''</ref> [[Lord]] [[Guattako]] was a warlord active on the planet [[Oosalon]] who attempted to assemble an [[Guattako's army|army]], forcefully recruiting children in the process, to bring his idea of freedom to his quadrant of the galaxy. His actions attracted the attention of [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Finis Valorum]], who dispatched members of the Jedi Order to bring Guattako to justice<ref name="Age of Republic">{{StoryCite|story=The Weapon|book=Age of Republic Special 1}}</ref> in [[34 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> While Guattako did battle with [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]], the warlord was taken by surprise and shot by one of the children he had kidnapped. With his death, the army was dissolved.<ref name="Age of Republic" />

===Clone Wars===
[[File:GrievousRevealsHimselfMygeeto-Kanan10.png|thumb|right|280px|General Grievous, cybernetic warlord of the CIS]]
The [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] made use of the position of warlord,<ref name="Weapons Factory" /> with holders of the rank including<ref name="Join the Battle">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref> its [[Supreme Martial Commander of the Separatist Droid Armies|Supreme Commander]],<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> the Kaleesh [[cyborg]] [[General]] Grievous,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> the same being who had, in his past, been a warlord of Kalee.<ref name="BDOWD" /> As a Separatist warlord<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and the government's Supreme Commander,<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> Grievous led the [[Confederacy military]] alongside [[Head of State]] [[Count]] [[Dooku]] and waged [[Clone Wars|war]] against the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Thrawn Alliances">''[[Thrawn: Alliances]]''</ref> Dooku was also considered a warlord.<ref name="backstories">''[[Darth Vader: Sith Lord]]''</ref> Other Confederate warlords were [[Archduke]] [[Poggle the Lesser]]<ref name="Weapons Factory" /> of the [[Stalgasin hive]]<ref name="Star Wars: On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref> and [[Karkarodon]] [[Commander]] [[Riff Tamson]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

Despite the peaceful ideals of the [[Jedi Order]],<ref name="AotC">{{Film|II}}</ref> its members would find themselves pressed into the role of Republic battlefield commanders for the war against the Separatists, with [[Jedi Knight]]s and [[Jedi Master|Masters]] assigned the rank of [[Jedi General]] under the [[Jedi Military Integration Act]].<ref name="Brotherhood">[[Brotherhood (novel)|''Brotherhood'']]</ref> One Jedi General, Master [[Pong Krell]],<ref name="Carnage of Krell">{{TCW|Carnage of Krell}}</ref> came to act as a warlord<ref name="Dave Filoni Luminara" /> and, ultimately, fell to the [[dark side of the Force]]. Krell hoped to join Dooku and serve as the count's new [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]], but his dreams were cut short by the [[clone trooper]]s whose trust he had abused: [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] rallied the [[501st Legion]] and [[212th Attack Battalion]] against the rogue Jedi, and Krell would then be executed by trooper [[Dogma]], who previously had been his most loyal follower.<ref name="Carnage of Krell" />

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Hollian, my second child. When I am gone, you will be the celebrant warlord, head of our war-faith. You will harvest the blood of those who stand against us.|The king of Shu-Torn, on Hollian's planned future|<ref name="DVA" />}}
[[File:DarthVader-BlackWhiteRed1-virginvariant-Suayan.jpg|thumb|left|270px|Darth Vader, warlord of the Empire]]
At the [[Mission to Mustafar|end of the Clone Wars]], the Republic was [[Proclamation of the New Order|transformed]] into the [[Galactic Empire]] by [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]], who, in part, made use of a massive [[Imperial Military]] to enforce his will.<ref name="Rise and Fall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> The [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]]&mdash;who, as [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]] to Palpatine, was allowed power<ref name="Dark Lord 12">[[Darth Vader (2017) 12|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 12]]</ref> over the Imperial Military comparable to that of a [[Commander-in-Chief]]<ref name="Bust Collection">{{BustCollectionCite|30|Star Wars Universe}}</ref>&mdash;acted as a warlord<ref name="Secret Jedi">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Jedi]]''</ref> for the Empire.<ref name="Dark Lord 12" /> [[Kaplan (Imperial)|Kaplan]] was a warlord of the Empire whose actions granted him a legacy in galactic history.<ref name="TFA VD" /> [[Burnium Ro]] was a warlord active in the [[Imperial Era]] who drew upon the imagery of the Nihil, creating a force<ref name="Star Wars 7">[[Star Wars (2020) 7|''Star Wars'' (2020) 7]]</ref> of self-styled Nihil holdouts.<ref name="Rise and Fall" />

The position of [[celebrant warlord]] existed within the [[Kingdom of Shu-Torun]], where they sat as head of the [[War-Faith]] and led conflict against the kingdom's enemies. During the days of [[Unidentified King of Shu-Torun|one king]], he sat as both [[Shu-Torun royal family|monarch]] and celebrant warlord, but he planned to pass down his crown to his eldest son [[Monthan]], while the warlord title would be assigned to his second eldest child<ref name="DVA" /> and current [[Shu-Torun war minister]],<ref name="Darth Vader 17">[[Darth Vader (2015) 17|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 17]]</ref> his daughter [[Hollian]]. The arrival of Vader, however, would result in the execution of the whole family aside from the king's youngest child, Princess [[Trios]],<ref name="DVA" /> who found herself inheriting every royal title and, thus, was both warlord and queen.<ref name="Darth Vader 16">[[Darth Vader (2015) 16|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 16]]</ref>

===After the Empire===
{{Quote|The Empire is gone, Mando. All that are left are mercenaries and warlords.|[[Greef Karga]], to [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="Chapter 3" />}}
[[File:AGE-KyloCover.png|thumb|right|270px|Kylo Ren, warlord of the First Order]]
Following their major loss in the [[Battle of Endor]], which saw the apparent [[death]] of [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] and the destruction of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station]], the Galactic Empire shattered into factionalism.<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref> After its fall in the [[Battle of Jakku]], the Empire<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref> was reduced to scattered warlords and [[Mercenary|mercenaries]].<ref name="Chapter 3" /> While most of them vowed to resurrect the Empire, many were more interested in carving fiefdoms out of the Empire's ashes.<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> The former [[stormtrooper]] [[Sentinel]] donned the "[[Imperial Warlord]]" armor set in the [[Grand Arena]] of the planet [[Vespaara]].<ref name="Hunters" />

In the years after the fall of the Empire,<ref name="Part Eight" /> [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]<ref name="Battles" /> and [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]] "Thrawn" served as warlords who planned to resurrect and lead the Empire themselves during their conflicts with the [[New Republic]].<ref name="Part Eight" /> Gideon was also a member of the [[Shadow Council (Imperial Remnants)|Shadow Council]], a grouping of Imperial Remnant warlords who worked together in secret and awaited Thrawn's return to make war against the New Republic.<ref name="Chapter 23">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 23: The Spies}}</ref> Having survived the action on [[Jakku]], the former Imperial strategist [[Teza Nasz]] later united one of the [[warrior clan]]s of [[Rattatak]] behind her as a warlord, having the strength and intelligence to maintain her position.<ref name="Resistance Reborn">''[[Resistance Reborn]]''</ref> Three [[Standard decade|decades]] after the Battle of Endor, [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] [[Destruction of the Jedi Temple|severed]] his ties with the [[Jedi Order]] and became the new Master of the [[Knights of Ren]], a warlord, and, ultimately, [[Supreme Leader]] of the [[First Order]].<ref name="Kylo Ren" />

==Behind the scenes==
The position of warlord<ref name="Secret Jedi" /> first appeared in ''[[Star Wars]]'' media through the character of Darth Vader, who made his [[canon]]ical debut in [[1977]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope]], itself the first ''Star Wars'' film.<ref name="ANH">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Canonically speaking, however, Vader was not identified as a warlord until the [[2019]] reference book''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Jedi]]''.<ref name="Secret Jedi" />

The audio description for the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']] available on [[Disney+]] incorrectly translates a quote from Poggle to be that he is sending his "warlords" to hide in the [[Geonosian catacombs|Geonosis catacombs]].<ref name="audio description Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> The film's subtitles instead state Poggle is saying he is sending his [[Warrior caste (Geonosian)|Geonosian warriors]] to the catacombs.<ref name="AotC" />

